---
title: Pancakes
yield: 8%pancakes
course: Dessert
locale: en
difficulty: Easy
---

Sift @plain or self-raising flour{110%g} and @salt{large pinch} into a bowl. Beat to a smooth creamy batter with the unbeaten @egg{1}, half the @milk{0.5%pint} and @butter{1%tbsp}(melted). Stir in the remaining milk.

Heat an #8 or 9" frying pan{} over medium heat. Add a little @vegetable oil{}. When hot pour in half a cup of batter mixture (just enough to coat base of pan thinly and evenly). Fry until golden brown. Turn over with fish slice or spatula. Cook second side until golden and mottled.

> To keep pancakes warm as they are being made, stack them on a plate over a pan of gently simmering water, covered with a large lid or second plate.

Serve with @caster sugar{} and @lemon juice{}.